ing in in those places  and you can see in May those patches are  are much smaller as we as we have more  and more data all right all right  so that's monthly now we're moving  towards weekly so this is only for the  continental US this is I believe 13  weeks of of weekly mosaics over the  continental United States and here you  can see some gaps those are almost  entirely due to clouds we're imaging  everything at least once a week in most  cases several times a week but there are  still some gaps in between where in that  week we never saw a clear view of the  ground but we're we're approaching now  we're averaging about 95% cloud free  coverage globally for the for the world  in a week so that's that's what we're  aiming for were and you know as the the  satellites spread out a little bit more  well we will improve that incrementally  there's a few other things we can do  operationally to help that but but we're  still limited by clouds essentially so  that that last few percent is is hard to  get  all right so let me wrap up with a few  other things I want to talk about some  of the things that were looking at at  doing next so I showed you an example of  weekly we're moving towards producing  those every week and globally and we  hope to have those as a product sometime  this year that's available to customers  another way to increase that frequency  is it's hard to do a daily purely time  windowed mosaic because of that cloud  issue that I showed you if you look at  just a snapshot of the earth on one day  it's 50% clouds so updating the the  daily mosaic every day just by finding  the good cloud free images and having a  dynamically generated image where you  have all the clear images from that day  and then you may go back the rest of the  week maybe even back farther in some  places have a dynamic mosaic that's  another another product that we are  working towards happening and then one  other thing is to use the fourth band to  use that NIR band and incorp